    "verdict": "FIBRE PER-PARITY ACTION TEST (accelerator prerequisite; scope-(a)). Splitting the D-ladder by k-parity (M2 split) and measuring each half's own least-term action on the fibre (interior N*, no Padé): odd-half action mid=0.36337 (spread 0.315, n=3); even-half action mid=0.29842 (spread 0.819, n=9); separation |A_odd-A_even|=0.064945 (rel 0.196). the plateaus are NOT cleanly flat-and-distinct at k<=31 (per-parity actions still drifting -> the two-level inputs are NOT resolvable at k=31 (a legitimate negative: the accelerator cannot be fed clean critical times from this length; more exact rungs or a genuine transseries fit is required)). Honest: does NOT confirm two clean actions; records what k=31 can and cannot support. Caveat: interior N* is modest, so optimal-truncation asymptotics are coarse. No fit; no c_k wired; nothing to production; no tier change."
